   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "This is Starship,",
    "the biggest rocket ever flown,",
    "about four hundred feet tall.",
    "Let's take it apart."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 6.67,
   "chunks": [
    "The bottom stage is Super Heavy:",
    "thirty-three Raptor engines,",
    "over eighteen million pounds of thrust",
    "at liftoff."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 13.75,
   "chunks": [
    "Inside, stainless-steel tanks",
    "hold super-cold liquid oxygen",
    "and liquid methane."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 19.37,
   "chunks": [
    "Each Raptor runs",
    "full-flow staged combustion:",
    "two preburners",
    "spin two turbopumps,",
    "then everything burns in the chamber",
    "and roars out the nozzle."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 28.9,
   "chunks": [
    "Why methane?",
    "It burns cleaner than kerosene,",
    "so engines can be reused.",
    "And SpaceX plans to make it on Mars."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 36.68,
   "chunks": [
    "At staging, the ship ignites",
    "through a vented ring.",
    "The booster flies home on grid fins,",
    "and the tower's arms catch it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 44.55,
   "chunks": [
    "The ship has six Raptors:",
    "three sea-level, three vacuum.",
    "Hex tiles shield it,",
    "and four flaps steer the fall."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 51.6,
   "chunks": [
    "In September, Flight 14",
    "reached orbit and released",
    "26 Starlink satellites",
    "from its payload bay."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 58.45,
   "chunks": [
    "Next, SpaceX says:",
    "refueling in orbit,",
    "a Moon lander for NASA,",
    "and then Mars.",
    "Cargo first, then crews,",
    "then a city."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 66.84,
   "chunks": [
    "What should we take apart next?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 69.03,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "the rocket built for Mars."
   ]
